2026-10-28T17:39:52.2843822Z {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgV3YSEbEAHutDDrfu9ZC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BK2FLL76Kg3YQgcMB8ZL6F","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6008,"cache_read_input_tokens":24869,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6008,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d65baac-d53e-489e-b690-ad96bbd5485b","uuid":"473efbd9-34b2-4d4e-99a0-347a514ebf21","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:39:52.281Z","request_id":"req_011CgV3YRuzN7UQ6ZGwfJPnJ"}
2026-10-28T17:39:52.3032267Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BK2FLL76Kg3YQgcMB8ZL6F","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 31,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/31\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"[Enhancement]: aws_ecs_service: support deployment_configuration.early_success_criteria\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"### Description\\n\\nAmazon ECS added early success criteria for rolling deployments. The `DeploymentConfiguration` API type now carries an `earlySuccessCriteria` member with `enable`, `healthyPercent` and `sourceServiceRevisionCleanup` (`BLOCKING` or `DEFERRED`). When enabled, ECS marks a rolling deployment successful once the configured percentage of new tasks is healthy, and with `DEFERRED` cleanup it drains the source service revision after the deployment completes instead of blocking on it. CloudFormation exposes this as `AWS::ECS::Service DeploymentEarlySuccessCriteria`.\\n\\n`aws_ecs_service` has no way to set this today. The `deployment_configuration` block supports `strategy`, `bake_time_in_minutes` and `lifecycle_hook`, but not `early_success_criteria`, so the setting cannot be managed by Terraform and any value set outside Terraform is not represented in state.\\n\\nUse case: services whose tasks use task scale-in protection and legitimately keep running for a long time after a deployment starts (queue workers draining multi-hour jobs). The AWS documentation for early success criteria recommends `DEFERRED` cleanup for exactly this case, so that CI/CD tooling with time limits is not blocked while the old revision drains.\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n- resource/aws_ecs_service\\n- data-source/aws_ecs_service\\n\\n### Potential Terraform Configuration\\n\\n```hcl\\nresource \\\"aws_ecs_service\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  # ...\\n\\n  deployment_configuration {\\n    strategy = \\\"ROLLING\\\"\\n\\n    early_success_criteria {\\n      enable                          = true\\n      healthy_percent                 = 100\\n      source_service_revision_cleanup = \\\"DEFERRED\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### References\\n\\n- https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/early-success-criteria.html\\n- https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/APIReference/API_DeploymentConfiguration.html\\n- https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-properties-ecs-service-deploymentearlysuccesscriteria.html\\n- botocore `ecs/2014-11-13/service-2.json` shape `DeploymentEarlySuccessCriteria`\\n\\n### Would you like to implement the enhancement?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\n7\t  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n8\t  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n9\t  \"labels\": [],\n10\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:09:38Z\",\n11\t  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-21T08:53:55Z\"\n12\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d65baac-d53e-489e-b690-ad96bbd5485b","uuid":"9e81e328-8337-4a3a-8ff1-0f888ddd9984","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:39:52.297Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"number\": 31,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/31\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"[Enhancement]: aws_ecs_service: support deployment_configuration.early_success_criteria\",\n  \"body\": \"### Description\\n\\nAmazon ECS added early success criteria for rolling deployments. The `DeploymentConfiguration` API type now carries an `earlySuccessCriteria` member with `enable`, `healthyPercent` and `sourceServiceRevisionCleanup` (`BLOCKING` or `DEFERRED`). When enabled, ECS marks a rolling deployment successful once the configured percentage of new tasks is healthy, and with `DEFERRED` cleanup it drains the source service revision after the deployment completes instead of blocking on it. CloudFormation exposes this as `AWS::ECS::Service DeploymentEarlySuccessCriteria`.\\n\\n`aws_ecs_service` has no way to set this today. The `deployment_configuration` block supports `strategy`, `bake_time_in_minutes` and `lifecycle_hook`, but not `early_success_criteria`, so the setting cannot be managed by Terraform and any value set outside Terraform is not represented in state.\\n\\nUse case: services whose tasks use task scale-in protection and legitimately keep running for a long time after a deployment starts (queue workers draining multi-hour jobs). The AWS documentation for early success criteria recommends `DEFERRED` cleanup for exactly this case, so that CI/CD tooling with time limits is not blocked while the old revision drains.\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n- resource/aws_ecs_service\\n- data-source/aws_ecs_service\\n\\n### Potential Terraform Configuration\\n\\n```hcl\\nresource \\\"aws_ecs_service\\\" \\\"example\\\" {\\n  # ...\\n\\n  deployment_configuration {\\n    strategy = \\\"ROLLING\\\"\\n\\n    early_success_criteria {\\n      enable                          = true\\n      healthy_percent                 = 100\\n      source_service_revision_cleanup = \\\"DEFERRED\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### References\\n\\n- https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/early-success-criteria.html\\n- https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/APIReference/API_DeploymentConfiguration.html\\n- https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-properties-ecs-service-deploymentearlysuccesscriteria.html\\n- botocore `ecs/2014-11-13/service-2.json` shape `DeploymentEarlySuccessCriteria`\\n\\n### Would you like to implement the enhancement?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\n  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"labels\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:09:38Z\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-21T08:53:55Z\"\n}","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BK2FLL76Kg3YQgcMB8ZL6F","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
