2026-10-28T17:39:53.6560804Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Re9VUFMVJjq8kN8aBrPPKb","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 31,\n    \"title\": \"[Enhancement]: aws_ecs_service: support deployment_configuration.early_success_criteria\",\n    \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n    \"labels_at_open\": []\n  },\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-21T08:53:55+00:00\",\n  \"form\": {\n    \"template\": \"Request an Enhancement\",\n    \"missing_required\": [],\n    \"empty_optional\": [],\n    \"used_form\": true\n  },\n  \"services\": {\n    \"resources_mentioned\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"aws_ecs_service\",\n        \"resource_exists\": true,\n        \"data_source_exists\": true,\n        \"service_label\": \"service/ecs\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"regex_labeler_would_apply\": [\n      \"service/ecs\"\n    ],\n    \"primary_service_label\": \"service/ecs\"\n  },\n  \"versions\": {\n    \"terraform\": null,\n    \"provider\": null,\n    \"latest_release\": \"6.65.0\",\n    \"latest_release_date\": \"2026-09-16\",\n    \"provider_status\": \"not_reported\",\n    \"newer_release_notes\": [],\n    \"newer_fixes\": []\n  },\n  \"similar_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 43431,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#43431\",\n      \"title\": \"r/aws_ecs_service: Support deployment configuration strategy\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"AWS has recently added support for blue green deployments using ECS as deployment controller. This is also the new recommended way to do blue green deployments. > Amazon ECS enables built-in blue/green deployments * [Announcement]( * [Blog post]( Request: Add support for deployment_configuration where you may configure strategy which can have value: ROLLING or blue_green. Example from AWS docs: \\\"d\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2025-07-17T13:12:08Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.275,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 44883,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#44883\",\n      \"title\": \"ECS - Linear and Canary deployments\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"Amazon ECS now supports built-in Linear and Canary deployments [link]( This will be a new addition to the deployment_configuration. * aws_ecs_service hcl resource \\\"aws_ecs_service\\\" \\\"example\\\" { name = \\\"example\\\" cluster = aws_ecs_cluster.example.id # ... other configurations ... deployment_configuration { strategy = \\\"CANARY\\\" bake_time_in_minutes = 15 canary_configuration { canary_percent = 10.0 cana\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2025-10-30T21:25:09Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.262,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 48075,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#48075\",\n      \"title\": \"Add target_type and timeout_configuration to lifecycle_hook in aws_ecs_service (pause hook support)\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"The ECS API now supports PAUSE lifecycle hooks (announced May 19, 2026), but the lifecycle_hook block in aws_ecs_service only exposes Lambda hook fields. The target_type and timeout_configuration attributes are missing, making it impossible to configure pause hooks via Terraform. - aws_ecs_service hcl resource \\\"aws_ecs_service\\\" \\\"example\\\" { # ... deployment_configuration { strategy = \\\"CANARY\\\" canar\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-05-27T04:25:23Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.183,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 32265,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#32265\",\n      \"title\": \"[Enhancement]: Add support for setting the deploymentConfiguration field on aws_ecs_service resources\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"This is a relatively new feature documented in this [blog]( post, which allows ECS to automatically rollback deployments in case of failures: Here's how the new parameter looks like in JSON, as per the above blog: \\\"deploymentConfiguration\\\":{ \\\"deploymentCircuitBreaker\\\":{ \\\"enable\\\":true, \\\"rollback\\\":true }, \\\"maximumPercent\\\":200, \\\"minimumHealthyPercent\\\":50, \\\"alarms\\\":{ \\\"alarmNames\\\":[ \\\"HighResponseLatenc\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"not_planned\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2023-06-28T18:34:11Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.174,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 45678,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#45678\",\n      \"title\": \"aws_ecs_service: Terraform triggered deployments do not alternate target groups for ECS-managed blue/green\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"aws_ecs_service When using ECS-managed blue/green deployments (deployment_controller = \\\"ECS\\\" with blue_green_deployment enabled), Terraform-managed updates to an aws_ecs_service should behave the same as deployments triggered manually via the AWS console. ECS should be able to: - Correctly determine the active and inactive target groups - Register new tasks to the inactive target group during a de\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2025-12-21T13:09:35Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.17,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"corpus_size\": 11718,\n  \"thresholds\": {\n    \"likely\": 0.4,\n    \"possible\": 0.28\n  }\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d65baac-d53e-489e-b690-ad96bbd5485b","uuid":"73fd6c22-fef1-47d0-ba3c-059232a11429","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:39:53.645Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 31,\n    \"title\": \"[Enhancement]: aws_ecs_service: support deployment_configuration.early_success_criteria\",\n    \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n    \"labels_at_open\": []\n  },\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-09-21T08:53:55+00:00\",\n  \"form\": {\n    \"template\": \"Request an Enhancement\",\n   